[2026-03-14T20:38:21.037Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018Fx5WPuTeuWrEoyiJdeA9K","type":"tool_result","content":"   800→- **Initial state**: User selected a connecting flight (LAX → DFW → JFK, 1 stop) from search results\n   801→- **Action**: User observes the FlightSummary section\n   802→- **Expected**: The itinerary displays both legs in order: Leg 1 (LAX → DFW) with its airline, flight number, departure/arrival times, terminal info, and duration; then a layover indicator showing layover duration and airport (e.g., \"2h 15m layover at DFW\"); then Leg 2 (DFW → JFK) with its details. The timeline visualization shows the full journey with the layover marked.\n   803→\n   804→#### Test: FlightSummary shows total duration and stops count\n   805→- **Components**: FlightSummary\n   806→- **Initial state**: User selected a 1-stop flight with total duration 8h 45m\n   807→- **Action**: User observes the FlightSummary header area\n   808→- **Expected**: A summary line displays the total journey duration \"8h 45m\" and the number of stops \"1 stop\". For nonstop flights, it shows \"Nonstop\".\n   809→\n   810→#### Test: FlightSummary shows overnight arrival indicator\n   811→- **Components**: FlightSummary\n   812→- **Initial state**: User selected a flight that arrives the next day (departs 11:00 PM, arrives 6:00 AM +1)\n   813→- **Action**: User observes the arrival time in FlightSummary\n   814→- **Expected**: The arrival time displays a \"+1\" indicator next to it, signaling the flight arrives the following day.\n   815→\n   816→#### Test: FlightSummary shows aircraft type and amenities\n   817→- **Components**: FlightSummary\n   818→- **Initial state**: User selected a flight with aircraft_type \"Boeing 737-800\", has_wifi=true, has_power=true, has_entertainment=false\n   819→- **Action**: User observes the flight leg details in FlightSummary\n   820→- **Expected**: The aircraft type \"Boeing 737-800\" is displayed. Amenity icons are shown: Wi-Fi icon (present), power outlet icon (present). Entertainment icon is not shown or shown as unavailable.\n   821→\n   822→#### Test: FlightSummary shows baggage allowance\n   823→- **Components**: FlightSummary\n   824→- **Initial state**: User selected a flight and the booking page is loaded\n   825→- **Action**: User observes the FlightSummary details\n   826→- **Expected**: Baggage allowance information is displayed for the selected cabin class (e.g., \"1 carry-on bag, 1 checked bag included\" for economy).\n   827→\n   828→### PriceBreakdown\n   829→\n   830→#### Test: PriceBreakdown displays base fare per passenger\n   831→- **Components**: PriceBreakdown\n   832→- **Initial state**: User selected a flight for 1 adult in economy class, base fare $250, taxes $45\n   833→- **Action**: User observes the PriceBreakdown section\n   834→- **Expected**: The breakdown shows a line item \"Base fare\" with \"$250\" for 1 adult. The line item is labeled with the passenger type \"Adult × 1\".\n   835→\n   836→#### Test: PriceBreakdown displays taxes and fees\n   837→- **Components**: PriceBreakdown\n   838→- **Initial state**: User selected a flight with taxes_cents = 4500\n   839→- **Action**: User observes the PriceBreakdown section\n   840→- **Expected**: A \"Taxes and fees\" line item shows \"$45.00\". The taxes are listed as a separate line from the base fare.\n   841→\n   842→#### Test: PriceBreakdown displays total price\n   843→- **Components**: PriceBreakdown\n   844→- **Initial state**: User selected a flight with base fare $250 and taxes $45\n   845→- **Action**: User observes the PriceBreakdown section\n   846→- **Expected**: A prominently displayed \"Total\" line shows \"$295.00\". It is visually distinct (bold, larger font, or separated by a divider) from the individual line items.\n   847→\n   848→#### Test: PriceBreakdown shows per-passenger-type pricing for mixed group\n   849→- **Components**: PriceBreakdown\n   850→- **Initial state**: User searched with 2 adults, 1 child, 1 infant and selected a flight\n   851→- **Action**: User observes the PriceBreakdown section\n   852→- **Expected**: The breakdown shows separate line items for each passenger type: \"Adult × 2\" with the per-adult base fare and subtotal, \"Child × 1\" with the child base fare, \"Infant × 1\" with the infant base fare. Taxes and fees are shown. The grand total sums all passengers.\n   853→\n   854→#### Test: PriceBreakdown updates for round-trip flights\n   855→- **Components**: PriceBreakdown\n   856→- **Initial state**: User selected a round-trip flight (outbound + return)\n   857→- **Action**: User observes the PriceBreakdown section\n   858→- **Expected**: The breakdown includes pricing for both the outbound and return flights. The total reflects the combined cost of both directions plus all taxes and fees.\n   859→\n   860→#### Test: PriceBreakdown reflects selected cabin class pricing\n   861→- **Components**: PriceBreakdown\n   862→- **Initial state**: User searched for Business class and selected a flight\n   863→- **Action**: User observes the PriceBreakdown section\n   864→- **Expected**: The cabin class \"Business\" is indicated in the breakdown. The base fare reflects the business class pricing (higher than economy). The total price matches the business class total_price_cents from the database.\n   865→\n   866→### PassengerForm\n   867→\n   868→#### Test: PassengerForm displays correct number of passenger forms\n   869→- **Components**: PassengerForm\n   870→- **Initial state**: User searched with 2 adults and 1 child, then selected a flight\n   871→- **Action**: User observes the PassengerForm section\n   872→- **Expected**: Three separate passenger sub-forms are displayed, labeled \"Passenger 1 (Adult)\", \"Passenger 2 (Adult)\", and \"Passenger 3 (Child)\". Each form has fields for first name, last name, date of birth, and gender.\n   873→\n   874→#### Test: PassengerForm shows primary passenger contact fields\n   875→- **Components**: PassengerForm\n   876→- **Initial state**: Booking page loaded with 2 adults\n   877→- **Action**: User observes Passenger 1 form\n   878→- **Expected**: Passenger 1 (primary passenger) has additional fields for email address and phone number that are not present on the other passenger forms.\n   879→\n   880→#### Test: PassengerForm first name and last name input\n   881→- **Components**: PassengerForm\n   882→- **Initial state**: Booking page loaded, passenger forms are empty\n   883→- **Action**: User types \"John\" in the first name field and \"Doe\" in the last name field of Passenger 1\n   884→- **Expected**: The first name field displays \"John\" and the last name field displays \"Doe\". The input is reflected in the form state.\n   885→\n   886→#### Test: PassengerForm date of birth picker\n   887→- **Components**: PassengerForm\n   888→- **Initial state**: Booking page loaded, Passenger 1 form visible\n   889→- **Action**: User clicks the date of birth field and selects a date (e.g., January 15, 1990)\n   890→- **Expected**: A date picker opens. After selecting the date, the field displays \"01/15/1990\" (or equivalent formatted date). The date picker closes.\n   891→\n   892→#### Test: PassengerForm gender dropdown\n   893→- **Components**: PassengerForm\n   894→- **Initial state**: Booking page loaded, Passenger 1 form visible\n   895→- **Action**: User clicks the gender dropdown\n   896→- **Expected**: A dropdown opens with options (e.g., \"Male\", \"Female\", \"Other\", \"Prefer not to say\"). Selecting an option updates the field and closes the dropdown.\n   897→\n   898→#### Test: PassengerForm email validation\n   899→- **Components**: PassengerForm\n   900→- **Initial state**: Booking page loaded, Passenger 1 form visible\n   901→- **Action**: User types \"invalid-email\" in the email field and attempts to submit\n   902→- **Expected**: A validation error appears on the email field indicating an invalid email format (e.g., \"Please enter a valid email address\"). The form does not submit.\n   903→\n   904→#### Test: PassengerForm email accepts valid input\n   905→- **Components**: PassengerForm\n   906→- **Initial state**: Booking page loaded, Passenger 1 form visible\n   907→- **Action**: User types \"john.doe@example.com\" in the email field\n   908→- **Expected**: The email field displays \"john.doe@example.com\" with no validation errors.\n   909→\n   910→#### Test: PassengerForm phone number input\n   911→- **Components**: PassengerForm\n   912→- **Initial state**: Booking page loaded, Passenger 1 form visible\n   913→- **Action**: User types \"+1 555-123-4567\" in the phone number field\n   914→- **Expected**: The phone number field accepts and displays the input. No validation error is shown.\n   915→\n   916→#### Test: PassengerForm required field validation\n   917→- **Components**: PassengerForm, BookingAction\n   918→- **Initial state**: Booking page loaded, all passenger forms are empty\n   919→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Book Flight\" button without filling in any fields\n   920→- **Expected**: Validation errors appear on all required fields (first name, last name, date of birth, gender for each passenger; email and phone for primary passenger). The booking is not submitted. Error messages indicate which fields are required.\n   921→\n   922→#### Test: PassengerForm infant passenger form\n   923→- **Components**: PassengerForm\n   924→- **Initial state**: User searched with 1 adult, 1 infant and selected a flight\n   925→- **Action**: User observes the passenger forms\n   926→- **Expected**: Two forms are displayed: \"Passenger 1 (Adult)\" with contact fields, and \"Passenger 2 (Infant)\" with first name, last name, date of birth, and gender but no email/phone fields.\n   927→\n   928→#### Test: PassengerForm can be filled and edited multiple times\n   929→- **Components**: PassengerForm\n   930→- **Initial state**: Booking page loaded, passenger form is empty\n   931→- **Action**: User fills in first name \"John\", then changes it to \"Jane\", interacts with date of birth picker, then returns to first name and changes it to \"Alex\"\n   932→- **Expected**: Each edit is correctly reflected in the form. The final state shows \"Alex\" in the first name field. Other fields retain their entered values between edits.\n   933→\n   934→### BookingAction\n   935→\n   936→#### Test: BookingAction displays \"Book Flight\" button\n   937→- **Components**: BookingAction\n   938→- **Initial state**: Booking page loaded with flight selected\n   939→- **Action**: User observes the BookingAction section\n   940→- **Expected**: A prominent \"Book Flight\" button is displayed. The button text reads \"Book Flight\" and is styled as a primary action button (blue background, white text).\n   941→\n   942→#### Test: BookingAction successfully books a flight\n   943→- **Components**: BookingAction, PassengerForm, PriceBreakdown\n   944→- **Initial state**: All passenger forms are filled out correctly (Passenger 1: John Doe, john@example.com, +1 555-123-4567, DOB 1990-01-15, Male)\n   945→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Book Flight\" button\n   946→- **Expected**: The booking is saved to the database. A confirmation message is displayed with a unique booking reference number (e.g., \"Booking confirmed! Reference: ABC123\"). The bookings table has a new row with status \"confirmed\", the correct flight_id, session_id, cabin_class, and total_price_cents. The booking_passengers table has corresponding passenger records.\n   947→\n   948→#### Test: BookingAction shows booking reference number\n   949→- **Components**: BookingAction\n   950→- **Initial state**: User has just successfully booked a flight\n   951→- **Action**: User observes the confirmation\n   952→- **Expected**: A booking reference number is prominently displayed (e.g., \"Your booking reference: GF-ABC123\"). The reference is unique and can be used to identify the booking in the My Trips page.\n   953→\n   954→#### Test: BookingAction prevents double booking\n   955→- **Components**: BookingAction\n   956→- **Initial state**: User has just successfully booked a flight and sees the confirmation\n   957→- **Action**: User attempts to click \"Book Flight\" again (e.g., via browser back or re-clicking)\n   958→- **Expected**: The button is either disabled after successful booking, or the system prevents duplicate bookings. No second booking is created in the database.\n   959→\n   960→#### Test: BookingAction shows loading state during submission\n   961→- **Components**: BookingAction\n   962→- **Initial state**: All passenger forms filled, user clicks \"Book Flight\"\n   963→- **Action**: User observes the button during submission\n   964→- **Expected**: The button shows a loading indicator (spinner or \"Booking...\" text) while the request is being processed. The button is disabled during this time to prevent multiple clicks.\n   965→\n   966→#### Test: BookingAction booking appears in My Trips\n   967→- **Components**: BookingAction, TripCard\n   968→- **Initial state**: User has just successfully booked a flight (LAX → JFK, Mar 25, Delta DL100, $295)\n   969→- **Action**: User navigates to the My Trips page\n   970→- **Expected**: The \"Upcoming\" tab shows the newly booked trip with route \"LAX → JFK\", date \"Mar 25\", airline \"Delta\", status badge \"Confirmed\", price \"$295\", and the booking reference number.\n   971→\n   972→#### Test: BookingAction handles booking error gracefully\n   973→- **Components**: BookingAction\n   974→- **Initial state**: All passenger forms filled, but a network or server error occurs during booking\n   975→- **Action**: User clicks \"Book Flight\" and the request fails\n   976→- **Expected**: An error message is displayed (e.g., \"Booking failed. Please try again.\"). The form data is preserved so the user does not need to re-enter information. The \"Book Flight\" button becomes clickable again.\n   977→\n   978→## Page: My Trips\n   979→\n   980→### Components\n   981→- TripsTabs\n   982→- TripCard\n   983→- TrackedRouteCard\n   984→- CancelBookingModal\n   985→\n   986→### TripsTabs\n   987→\n   988→#### Test: TripsTabs displays three tabs\n   989→- **Components**: TripsTabs\n   990→- **Initial state**: User navigates to the My Trips page\n   991→- **Action**: User observes the tab bar at the top of the page\n   992→- **Expected**: Three tabs are displayed: \"Upcoming\", \"Past\", and \"Tracked\". The \"Upcoming\" tab is selected by default and visually highlighted (e.g., underline or bold text with primary color #1A73E8).\n   993→\n   994→#### Test: TripsTabs switches to Past tab\n   995→- **Components**: TripsTabs, TripCard\n   996→- **Initial state**: My Trips page loaded with \"Upcoming\" tab active, user has both upcoming and past bookings\n   997→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Past\" tab\n   998→- **Expected**: The \"Past\" tab becomes visually selected. The content area updates to show only trips with past departure dates (status \"Completed\" or \"Cancelled\"). Upcoming trips are no longer visible.\n   999→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01KeobCDh8fWJYJx3S5W95f3","session_id":"caed05c8-a48c-4a20-945a-0c006d1f37c2","uuid":"f3f6037a-6d2a-445e-8ffd-2b9e997a2b8a"}
