[2026-03-14T20:38:21.209Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Fvninsr4T5jwBJWynuj6zS","type":"tool_result","content":"  1000→#### Test: TripsTabs switches to Tracked tab\n  1001→- **Components**: TripsTabs, TrackedRouteCard\n  1002→- **Initial state**: My Trips page loaded with \"Upcoming\" tab active, user has tracked routes\n  1003→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Tracked\" tab\n  1004→- **Expected**: The \"Tracked\" tab becomes visually selected. The content area updates to show tracked route cards instead of trip cards. Trip cards are no longer visible.\n  1005→\n  1006→#### Test: TripsTabs switches back to Upcoming after visiting other tabs\n  1007→- **Components**: TripsTabs, TripCard\n  1008→- **Initial state**: User is on My Trips page viewing the \"Tracked\" tab\n  1009→- **Action**: User clicks \"Past\" tab, then clicks \"Upcoming\" tab\n  1010→- **Expected**: Each tab click updates the selected tab styling and displayed content correctly. After returning to \"Upcoming\", only upcoming trips are shown with the \"Upcoming\" tab visually selected.\n  1011→\n  1012→#### Test: TripsTabs Upcoming tab shows empty state\n  1013→- **Components**: TripsTabs, TripCard\n  1014→- **Initial state**: User has no upcoming bookings\n  1015→- **Action**: User views the \"Upcoming\" tab on My Trips page\n  1016→- **Expected**: An empty state message is displayed (e.g., \"No upcoming trips. Search for flights to plan your next trip!\"). No trip cards are shown.\n  1017→\n  1018→#### Test: TripsTabs Past tab shows empty state\n  1019→- **Components**: TripsTabs, TripCard\n  1020→- **Initial state**: User has no past bookings\n  1021→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Past\" tab\n  1022→- **Expected**: An empty state message is displayed (e.g., \"No past trips yet.\"). No trip cards are shown.\n  1023→\n  1024→#### Test: TripsTabs Tracked tab shows empty state\n  1025→- **Components**: TripsTabs, TrackedRouteCard\n  1026→- **Initial state**: User has no tracked routes\n  1027→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Tracked\" tab\n  1028→- **Expected**: An empty state message is displayed (e.g., \"No tracked routes. Use the 'Track prices' button on search results to start tracking.\"). No tracked route cards are shown.\n  1029→\n  1030→#### Test: TripsTabs Upcoming tab sorts trips by departure date ascending\n  1031→- **Components**: TripsTabs, TripCard\n  1032→- **Initial state**: User has 3 upcoming bookings with departure dates Mar 25, Apr 10, and Mar 30\n  1033→- **Action**: User views the \"Upcoming\" tab\n  1034→- **Expected**: Trip cards are sorted by departure date ascending: Mar 25 first, Mar 30 second, Apr 10 third. The soonest departure is at the top.\n  1035→\n  1036→### TripCard\n  1037→\n  1038→#### Test: TripCard displays route information\n  1039→- **Components**: TripCard\n  1040→- **Initial state**: User has an upcoming booking from LAX to JFK\n  1041→- **Action**: User observes a trip card in the Upcoming tab\n  1042→- **Expected**: The card displays the route as \"LAX → JFK\" showing the origin and destination airport IATA codes.\n  1043→\n  1044→#### Test: TripCard displays travel dates\n  1045→- **Components**: TripCard\n  1046→- **Initial state**: User has a round-trip booking departing Mar 25, returning Mar 30\n  1047→- **Action**: User observes the trip card\n  1048→- **Expected**: The card displays the departure date \"Mar 25\" and return date \"Mar 30\". For one-way trips, only the departure date is shown.\n  1049→\n  1050→#### Test: TripCard displays airline and flight info\n  1051→- **Components**: TripCard\n  1052→- **Initial state**: User has a booking on Delta flight DL100\n  1053→- **Action**: User observes the trip card\n  1054→- **Expected**: The card shows the airline name \"Delta\" and flight number \"DL100\". The airline logo (colored circle with airline initials) is displayed.\n  1055→\n  1056→#### Test: TripCard displays Confirmed status badge\n  1057→- **Components**: TripCard\n  1058→- **Initial state**: User has an upcoming confirmed booking\n  1059→- **Action**: User observes the trip card status\n  1060→- **Expected**: A status badge reading \"Confirmed\" is displayed on the card. The badge has a visual style indicating active status (e.g., green or blue background with white text).\n  1061→\n  1062→#### Test: TripCard displays Completed status badge\n  1063→- **Components**: TripCard\n  1064→- **Initial state**: User views the Past tab with a completed trip\n  1065→- **Action**: User observes the trip card status\n  1066→- **Expected**: A status badge reading \"Completed\" is displayed. The badge has a distinct style from Confirmed (e.g., gray background).\n  1067→\n  1068→#### Test: TripCard displays Cancelled status badge\n  1069→- **Components**: TripCard\n  1070→- **Initial state**: User views trips that include a cancelled booking\n  1071→- **Action**: User observes the cancelled trip card\n  1072→- **Expected**: A status badge reading \"Cancelled\" is displayed. The badge has a distinct style (e.g., red or muted background) indicating the trip was cancelled.\n  1073→\n  1074→#### Test: TripCard displays price paid\n  1075→- **Components**: TripCard\n  1076→- **Initial state**: User has a booking with total_price_cents = 29500\n  1077→- **Action**: User observes the trip card\n  1078→- **Expected**: The card displays the price as \"$295.00\" prominently on the card.\n  1079→\n  1080→#### Test: TripCard displays booking reference\n  1081→- **Components**: TripCard\n  1082→- **Initial state**: User has a booking with booking_reference \"GF-ABC123\"\n  1083→- **Action**: User observes the trip card\n  1084→- **Expected**: The booking reference \"GF-ABC123\" is displayed on the card so the user can identify and reference their booking.\n  1085→\n  1086→#### Test: TripCard shows cancel button for upcoming confirmed flights\n  1087→- **Components**: TripCard, CancelBookingModal\n  1088→- **Initial state**: User has an upcoming confirmed booking\n  1089→- **Action**: User observes the trip card in the Upcoming tab\n  1090→- **Expected**: A \"Cancel\" button is visible on the card. The button is styled as a secondary/destructive action (e.g., red text or outline).\n  1091→\n  1092→#### Test: TripCard does not show cancel button for past flights\n  1093→- **Components**: TripCard\n  1094→- **Initial state**: User views the Past tab with completed trips\n  1095→- **Action**: User observes trip cards in the Past tab\n  1096→- **Expected**: No \"Cancel\" button is shown on any trip card in the Past tab. Completed and past trips cannot be cancelled.\n  1097→\n  1098→#### Test: TripCard does not show cancel button for already cancelled flights\n  1099→- **Components**: TripCard\n  1100→- **Initial state**: User has a cancelled booking visible in any tab\n  1101→- **Action**: User observes the cancelled trip card\n  1102→- **Expected**: No \"Cancel\" button is shown. The card only displays the \"Cancelled\" status badge.\n  1103→\n  1104→#### Test: TripCard displays one-way trip correctly\n  1105→- **Components**: TripCard\n  1106→- **Initial state**: User has a one-way booking from SFO to ORD on Apr 5\n  1107→- **Action**: User observes the trip card\n  1108→- **Expected**: The card shows route \"SFO → ORD\", a single departure date \"Apr 5\", and no return date. All other fields (airline, price, status, reference) are displayed normally.\n  1109→\n  1110→#### Test: TripCard displays round-trip with return flight info\n  1111→- **Components**: TripCard\n  1112→- **Initial state**: User has a round-trip booking LAX → JFK departing Mar 25, returning Mar 30\n  1113→- **Action**: User observes the trip card\n  1114→- **Expected**: The card shows route \"LAX → JFK\", both dates \"Mar 25 – Mar 30\", and all booking details. The card indicates it is a round-trip booking.\n  1115→\n  1116→### TrackedRouteCard\n  1117→\n  1118→#### Test: TrackedRouteCard displays route\n  1119→- **Components**: TrackedRouteCard\n  1120→- **Initial state**: User has a tracked route from LAX to LHR, visible in the Tracked tab\n  1121→- **Action**: User observes the tracked route card\n  1122→- **Expected**: The card displays the route as \"LAX → LHR\" with origin and destination airport codes.\n  1123→\n  1124→#### Test: TrackedRouteCard displays date range being tracked\n  1125→- **Components**: TrackedRouteCard\n  1126→- **Initial state**: User tracks a route with departure_date_start \"2026-04-01\" and departure_date_end \"2026-04-15\"\n  1127→- **Action**: User observes the tracked route card\n  1128→- **Expected**: The card displays the tracked date range as \"Apr 1 – Apr 15\" (or similar formatted date range).\n  1129→\n  1130→#### Test: TrackedRouteCard displays current lowest price\n  1131→- **Components**: TrackedRouteCard\n  1132→- **Initial state**: User has a tracked route and there are flights available on that route with the lowest price being $320\n  1133→- **Action**: User observes the tracked route card\n  1134→- **Expected**: The card displays the current lowest price as \"$320\" prominently.\n  1135→\n  1136→#### Test: TrackedRouteCard displays price trend indicator going up\n  1137→- **Components**: TrackedRouteCard\n  1138→- **Initial state**: User has a tracked route where prices have increased by 12% compared to when tracking started\n  1139→- **Action**: User observes the tracked route card price trend\n  1140→- **Expected**: An upward arrow icon is displayed with \"+12%\" text next to the current price, indicating prices have risen. The trend indicator is styled in a color indicating increase (e.g., red).\n  1141→\n  1142→#### Test: TrackedRouteCard displays price trend indicator going down\n  1143→- **Components**: TrackedRouteCard\n  1144→- **Initial state**: User has a tracked route where prices have decreased by 8% compared to when tracking started\n  1145→- **Action**: User observes the tracked route card price trend\n  1146→- **Expected**: A downward arrow icon is displayed with \"-8%\" text next to the current price, indicating prices have dropped. The trend indicator is styled in a color indicating decrease (e.g., green).\n  1147→\n  1148→#### Test: TrackedRouteCard Search button navigates to search results\n  1149→- **Components**: TrackedRouteCard\n  1150→- **Initial state**: User has a tracked route LAX → LHR, Apr 1 – Apr 15\n  1151→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Search\" button on the tracked route card\n  1152→- **Expected**: The user is navigated to the Search Results page with the route (LAX → LHR) and date range (Apr 1 – Apr 15) pre-populated. Current flights for this route are displayed.\n  1153→\n  1154→#### Test: TrackedRouteCard Untrack button removes tracking\n  1155→- **Components**: TrackedRouteCard\n  1156→- **Initial state**: User has 2 tracked routes in the Tracked tab\n  1157→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Untrack\" button on one of the tracked route cards\n  1158→- **Expected**: The tracked route is removed from the database (tracked_routes table). The card is removed from the Tracked tab. Only 1 tracked route card remains. No confirmation modal is shown for untracking.\n  1159→\n  1160→#### Test: TrackedRouteCard Untrack then re-check shows updated list\n  1161→- **Components**: TrackedRouteCard, TripsTabs\n  1162→- **Initial state**: User has 3 tracked routes in the Tracked tab\n  1163→- **Action**: User clicks \"Untrack\" on the first card, then switches to \"Upcoming\" tab and back to \"Tracked\" tab\n  1164→- **Expected**: The Tracked tab consistently shows only 2 remaining tracked route cards. The untracked route does not reappear.\n  1165→\n  1166→#### Test: TrackedRouteCard Search button works for multiple cards\n  1167→- **Components**: TrackedRouteCard\n  1168→- **Initial state**: User has 2 tracked routes: LAX → LHR and SFO → NRT\n  1169→- **Action**: User clicks \"Search\" on the SFO → NRT card, navigates back to My Trips, then clicks \"Search\" on the LAX → LHR card\n  1170→- **Expected**: Each \"Search\" click navigates to the Search Results page with the correct route and dates pre-populated for that specific tracked route. The second search correctly shows LAX → LHR results, not the previous SFO → NRT search.\n  1171→\n  1172→### CancelBookingModal\n  1173→\n  1174→#### Test: CancelBookingModal opens when Cancel button is clicked\n  1175→- **Components**: CancelBookingModal, TripCard\n  1176→- **Initial state**: User has an upcoming confirmed booking in the Upcoming tab\n  1177→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Cancel\" button on the trip card\n  1178→- **Expected**: A modal dialog opens with a confirmation message (e.g., \"Are you sure you want to cancel this booking?\"). The modal displays the booking details: route, dates, airline, and booking reference. The modal has two buttons: \"Cancel Booking\" (destructive/confirm action) and \"Keep Booking\" (dismiss action).\n  1179→\n  1180→#### Test: CancelBookingModal shows booking details\n  1181→- **Components**: CancelBookingModal, TripCard\n  1182→- **Initial state**: User clicks Cancel on a booking LAX → JFK, Mar 25, Delta DL100, ref GF-ABC123\n  1183→- **Action**: User observes the modal content\n  1184→- **Expected**: The modal displays the specific booking details: route \"LAX → JFK\", date \"Mar 25\", airline \"Delta DL100\", booking reference \"GF-ABC123\". This helps the user confirm they are cancelling the correct booking.\n  1185→\n  1186→#### Test: CancelBookingModal confirms cancellation\n  1187→- **Components**: CancelBookingModal, TripCard\n  1188→- **Initial state**: Cancel modal is open for an upcoming booking\n  1189→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Cancel Booking\" button in the modal\n  1190→- **Expected**: The booking status is updated to \"cancelled\" in the database. The modal closes. The trip card updates to show a \"Cancelled\" status badge. The \"Cancel\" button is no longer visible on that trip card. The trip card remains visible in the list.\n  1191→\n  1192→#### Test: CancelBookingModal dismiss keeps booking\n  1193→- **Components**: CancelBookingModal, TripCard\n  1194→- **Initial state**: Cancel modal is open for an upcoming booking\n  1195→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Keep Booking\" button in the modal\n  1196→- **Expected**: The modal closes. The booking remains unchanged with status \"Confirmed\". The trip card still shows the \"Confirmed\" badge and the \"Cancel\" button is still available.\n  1197→\n  1198→#### Test: CancelBookingModal close via overlay click\n  1199→- **Components**: CancelBookingModal"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01KeobCDh8fWJYJx3S5W95f3","session_id":"caed05c8-a48c-4a20-945a-0c006d1f37c2","uuid":"5b3df98b-222a-4de0-abe6-ef8c05f417c3"}
